{"title":"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many ordered quadruples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/8/eb8c31b328eb3b0252134a4720e161c0fdf641e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a, b, c, d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> of positive integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e29ccfffe97ca4a463407c8f5354c8c19243b8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d \\leq 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> equal to the product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />? (That is, for how many such ordered quadruples is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/413a33cc9e77e5025eb2b687831b3dfe70678fb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc=d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" />?)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has prime factorization\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/f/21febf0dbff9209d3487b6b6116379b77cdd94da.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[d = p_1^{e_1} p_2^{e_2} \\cdots p_k^{e_k}\\]\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" />\nwith <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e01486dcc7cb25518b89692706b17389dc67c92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e8bc2235f5b0094bc37f2ef74f7dc647f0a406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/4508393135451dc6c41b01f36072dd16674586bc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"11\" /> prime numbers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f814fcbba7b623f656f7ce45b87262a9cf562dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/5/1353a34d24e4772061cc8654ee881fed3bd6ab02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/64683f315744c851898c8d65dace1a8aa31b93ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dots$\" width=\"19\" height=\"2\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/8545b9c0781ede672a8465beb72d9a8a9d7aebd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> positive integers. Then we must distribute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/1/f814fcbba7b623f656f7ce45b87262a9cf562dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e01486dcc7cb25518b89692706b17389dc67c92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/5/1353a34d24e4772061cc8654ee881fed3bd6ab02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e8bc2235f5b0094bc37f2ef74f7dc647f0a406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, and so on onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. If we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71cdc720659178ec2fe7d91811ee49679e156f6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{p_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"26\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/1833592afe33517f4ec6562241e517f1e6cfb447.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_{p_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"19\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/3/6438260469a05720a1a52ed179f36eecc434bdb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_{p_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> represent the number of prime factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e01486dcc7cb25518b89692706b17389dc67c92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" /> we assign to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, respectively, then we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/e/c1e542909580a428c8e24b893019a515be29f8bc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{p_1} + b_{p_1} + c_{p_1} = e_1,\\]\" width=\"156\" height=\"18\" />\nand by stars and bars, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc03a62288b8edaa701bd1b11750892cc275db94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{e_1+2}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"77\" height=\"55\" /> solutions. We can use similar reasoning on the other prime factors, so the number of solutions to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b3edc215f23665da7cfb91268d6cfb18499b226.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc = d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a05a9f5ce2d7689828a10a4f6d595499f76ebe46.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{e_1+2}{2} \\binom{e_2+2}{2} \\cdots \\binom{e_k+2}{2}\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/539ad518a65718ec2fb192a37ac084a327ff31f6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] usepackage(&quot;amsmath&quot;); unitsize(0.5cm); defaultpen(fontsize(10pt));  // Table layout real col1 = 2.1; real col2 = 6.5; real col3 = 14.5; real rowHeight = 1.3; int nRows = 10; // header + 8 data rows + total  real x0 = 0; real x1 = col1; real x2 = col1 + col2; real x3 = col1 + col2 + col3; real topY = 0; real bottomY = -nRows * rowHeight;  // Draw vertical lines draw((x0, topY)--(x0, bottomY)); draw((x1, topY)--(x1, bottomY)); draw((x2, topY)--(x2, bottomY)); draw((x3, topY)--(x3, bottomY));  // Draw horizontal lines for(int i = 0; i &lt;= nRows; ++i) {   real y = -i * rowHeight;   draw((x0, y)--(x3, y)); }  // Helper to place centered text in a cell void cellText(string s, int row, int col) {   real xleft, xright;   if(col == 0) { xleft = x0; xright = x1; }   else if(col == 1) { xleft = x1; xright = x2; }   else { xleft = x2; xright = x3; }   real ytop = -row * rowHeight;   real ybottom = -(row+1) * rowHeight;   label(s, ((xleft+xright)/2, (ytop+ybottom)/2)); }  // Header row cellText(&quot;$d$&quot;, 0, 0); cellText(&quot;prime factorization&quot;, 0, 1); cellText(&quot;number of ordered quadruples $(a,b,c,d)$&quot;, 0, 2);  // Data rows string[] dvals = {&quot;$1$&quot;, &quot;$2$&quot;, &quot;$3$&quot;, &quot;$4$&quot;, &quot;$5$&quot;, &quot;$6$&quot;, &quot;$7$&quot;, &quot;$8$&quot;}; string[] facts = {&quot;$1$&quot;, &quot;$2$&quot;, &quot;$3$&quot;, &quot;$2^2$&quot;, &quot;$5$&quot;, &quot;$2\\cdot 3$&quot;, &quot;$7$&quot;, &quot;$2^3$&quot;}; string[] counts = {   &quot;$1$&quot;,   &quot;$\\binom{1+2}{2}=3$&quot;,   &quot;$\\binom{1+2}{2}=3$&quot;,   &quot;$\\binom{2+2}{2}=6$&quot;,   &quot;$\\binom{1+2}{2}=3$&quot;,   &quot;$\\binom{1+2}{2}\\binom{1+2}{2}=9$&quot;,   &quot;$\\binom{1+2}{2}=3$&quot;,   &quot;$\\binom{3+2}{2}=10$&quot; };  for(int i = 0; i &lt; 8; ++i) {   cellText(dvals[i], i+1, 0);   cellText(facts[i], i+1, 1);   cellText(counts[i], i+1, 2); }  // Total row cellText(&quot;Total&quot;, 9, 0); cellText(&quot;&quot;, 9, 1); cellText(&quot;$\\boxed{38}$&quot;, 9, 2); [/asy]\" width=\"548\" height=\"308\" />\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC\" title=\"2024 CSMC\">2024 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3\" title=\"2024 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Senior Competition\">CEMC Senior Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018065717\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 182/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 134/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8279/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.711      1 Template:CEMC_CIMC/CSMC_box\n100.00%    7.711      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37541:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018065717 and revision id 290092. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}